{
  "id": "stimulus-sampling",
  "term": "stimulus sampling",
  "definition": "Stimulus sampling is the way test stimuli are selected across trials in a detection task. In this context, it means choosing signal intensities broadly across the psychometric function instead of concentrating on one response level, so sensitivity and decision-related influences can be estimated separately.",
